"""Draft seven SMR and five HEIDI primary-source role reviews; preserve literal thresholds and reuse distinctions."""
import argparse,gzip,hashlib,json,xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
from pathlib import Path
from setup_deseq2_reference import ROOT,pin,save
from collect_omics_review import paragraphs,validate_supporting_evidence
from dndscv_catalog import load_catalog_registry

SPECS=[
('P072','smr',25,[9],None,'previous-multi-SNP-result-reuse','Used previously completed European-only multi-SNP SMR results for44 selected genes near novel Parkinson disease loci, restricting tissues and applying FDR0.05 plus removal of signals with reported HEIDI P<0.05.','The source explicitly describes searching an existing result list; do not claim a fresh multi-SNP run in this paper. Methylation/expression inputs, prior LD/reference and original runtime remain separate. The exact SMR release is unspecified; do not infer an executable or reinterpret the reused results as a new cohort fit.'),
('P107','smr',24,[],None,'stratified-multi-SNP-expression-association','Applied SMR to APOE-stratified GWAS and five MetaBrain brain regions, using multi-SNP P<6.12e-6 for8166 unique genes and requiring HEIDI P>0.01 with reported nsnp_HEIDI>3.','The exact release and multi-SNP fitting options are unspecified despite the stated defaults. The count filter uses the reported HEIDI SNP-count column and is stricter than simply requesting a minimum of3. Multiple regions, APOE strata and the declared8166-gene correction family must remain explicit; a non-significant heterogeneity result does not establish causality.'),
('P107','heidi',24,[],None,'multi-SNP-result-heterogeneity-screen','Screened SMR results from the APOE-stratified MetaBrain analyses at HEIDI P>0.01 and retained only outputs with nsnp_HEIDI>3.','The paper describes this as removal of inferred pleiotropy; retain its wording without turning failure to reject heterogeneity into proof of a causal or pleiotropic mechanism. The SMR release, HEIDI mode, LD panel and exact instrument-selection options are unspecified.'),
('P150','smr',59,[60],'1.03','discovery-validation-tissue-association','Prioritized genes using SMR1.03 with brain, blood and other tissue cis-eQTL discovery datasets and separate validation datasets; corrected within each tested cohort and followed with HEIDI.','Paragraph60 specifies LD from10000 European-ancestry UKB individuals and cohort-wise Bonferroni correction. This reference and each tissue/cohort are caller inputs; do not substitute a generic LD panel or merge correction families. Source1.3.1/1.4.3 is not the reported1.03 runtime.'),
('P150','heidi',60,[59],None,'cohort-wise-linkage-heterogeneity-screen','Applied HEIDI to the genes resulting from cohort-wise Bonferroni-significant SMR analyses, using UKB-derived LD and reported P>0.05 screening.','The preceding paragraph names SMR1.03, not a separately versioned HEIDI package. Preserve its10000-person European LD reference and the paper wording about linkage/pleiotropy. Non-rejection is not confirmation of a single causal mechanism; HEIDI method and individual pruning arguments are not specified.'),
('P169','smr',43,[],'1.3.1','colon-eQTL-meta-summary-association','Ran SMR1.3.1 on meta-analyzed SOCCS/GTEx colon eQTL and colorectal-cancer GWAS summaries, corrected SMR P within each risk locus and retained corrected P<0.05 with HEIDI P>0.05; repeated the workflow for meta-analyzed tumor eQTL summaries.','Matrix eQTL residual adjustment, the0.5-Mb lead-variant and1-Mb gene windows, MAF filtering and inverse-variance meta-analysis are upstream of the SMR input. They do not declare SMR cis-window arguments. The paper cites defaults without fixing the exact binary, HEIDI mode or LD panel; preserve normal/tumor and risk-locus families.'),
('P183','smr',19,[],None,'single-and-multi-SNP-ncRNA-association','Integrated eQTL and GWAS summaries using top cis-eQTL SMR at eQTL P<5e-8 and a separate multi-SNP analysis with a500-kb window and stated LD pruning; used Bonferroni correction and HEIDI P>0.01.','The source supplies LD from8652 unrelated HRS individuals and reports multi-SNP pruning at r2>0.1. Preserve the actual selected populations and the two SMR modes. COLOC, FUSION and OPERA have separate methods and exclusions; their priors, prediction training and multi-exposure HEIDI are not ordinary SMR/HEIDI defaults. The release is unspecified.'),
('P183','heidi',19,[],None,'cis-eQTL-heterogeneity-screen','Applied HEIDI using three to20 cis-eQTL SNPs, reported eQTL P<1.57e-8 and LD bounds0.05–0.9, and required HEIDI P>0.01 alongside Bonferroni-significant SMR.','Retain the literal1.57e-8 threshold; it differs from the commonly documented1.57e-3 default and must not be silently corrected. The reference is the stated8652-person HRS panel. OPERA multi-exposure HEIDI is separate from this ordinary HEIDI screen; the runtime release/mode are unspecified.'),
('P189','smr',12,[29],None,'supplementary-protein-trait-association','Used SMR as a supplementary association analysis after primary plasma-protein Mendelian-randomization findings for PCOS, with SMR P<0.05 and a separate HEIDI screen.','This is downstream validation of selected primary MR findings, not a replacement for the original Wald/IVW, colocalization, discovery/replication or therapeutic-target tiering analyses. Paragraph29 reports testing65 proteins; keep that selected population and avoid interpreting software output alone as biological causality. Version, LD reference and detailed SMR options are unspecified.'),
('P189','heidi',12,[29],None,'supplementary-protein-linkage-screen','Used HEIDI to investigate whether protein–PCOS associations reflected distinct linked variants; reported P<0.05 as heterogeneity evidence and P>0.05 as the pass criterion in the results.','Retain the two reported strict inequalities and the selected65-protein population. A non-significant result is not proof of causality or absence of linkage. Replication, colocalization and druggability tiers are separate downstream decisions; runtime, LD panel, mode and SNP-selection parameters are unspecified.'),
('P203','smr',28,[],None,'non-European-schizophrenia-gene-prioritization','Applied SMR to significant QTL summaries filtered at FDR<0.05 and schizophrenia GWAS summaries filtered at P<5e-8, then required Bonferroni-significant SMR and HEIDI P>0.05.','The input filtering and correction family are explicit study choices, not general SMR defaults. The paper calls its SMR P empirical but does not describe a permutation implementation; do not relabel an asymptotic chi-square probability as empirically calibrated. Version, LD reference and exact options are unspecified.'),
('P203','heidi',28,[],None,'non-European-gene-heterogeneity-screen','Included the default-described SMR HEIDI test and retained prioritized schizophrenia genes with HEIDI P>0.05 together with Bonferroni-significant SMR.','The paper calls the0.05 HEIDI threshold an LD cutoff; it is a reported test-P condition, not a stated r2 pruning threshold. Do not infer an LD bound, runtime version or reference population, and do not treat non-rejection as proof of a causal mechanism.')
]


def main():
    p=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__);p.add_argument('--out',required=True,type=Path);a=p.parse_args();out=a.out.resolve();assert out.is_relative_to(ROOT/'build/literature-review/smr-runtime') and not out.exists();out.mkdir(parents=True);papers={p['paper_id']:p for p in json.loads((ROOT/'docs/literature/omics-2023-2026/papers.json').read_bytes())};registry={r['id']:r for r in load_catalog_registry(ROOT)};drafts=[];sources={};prior=json.loads((ROOT/'tools/literature/reviewed-uses.json').read_bytes());assert not any(r['tool_id'] in ['smr','heidi'] for r in prior['reviews'])
    for pid,tool,index,support,version,context,summary,scope in SPECS:
        paper=papers[pid];raw=gzip.decompress((ROOT/'build/literature-review/xml'/(paper['pmcid']+'.xml.gz')).read_bytes());assert hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()==paper['xml_sha256'];tree=ET.fromstring(raw);assert next(e.text for e in tree.findall('front/article-meta/article-id') if e.get('pub-id-type')=='doi').lower()==paper['doi'].lower();ps=paragraphs(tree);by={p['paragraph_index']:p for p in ps};obs=next(t for t in paper['tools'] if t['tool_id']==tool);primary=by[index];sha=hashlib.sha256(primary['text'].encode('utf8')).hexdigest();assert obs['evidence_paragraph_index']==index and obs['evidence_paragraph_sha256']==sha;supporting=[dict(paragraph_index=i,section=by[i]['section'],paragraph_sha256=hashlib.sha256(by[i]['text'].encode('utf8')).hexdigest()) for i in support]
        if pid=='P150' and tool=='heidi':supporting[0].update(evidence_role='method-details',named_anchor=dict(paragraph_index=index,section=primary['section'],paragraph_sha256=sha),shared_terms=['SMR','genes'],relation_note='The preceding paragraph declares SMR1.03 for the gene-prioritization analyses whose resulting genes are subjected to HEIDI in the named paragraph60; this identifies the shared workflow context, not a separate HEIDI version.')
        review=dict(pmcid=paper['pmcid'],doi=paper['doi'],tool_id=tool,evidence_paragraph_sha256=sha,use_summary=summary,implementation_scope_note=scope,version_reported_near_name=version,usage_context=context,supporting_evidence=supporting);validate_supporting_evidence(ps,[review],registry);drafts.append(dict(paper_id=pid,primary_paragraph=index,section=primary['section'],review=review,xml_sha256=paper['xml_sha256']));sources[pid+'/'+tool]=dict(primary=primary,supporting=[by[i] for i in support])
    assert len(drafts)==12 and sum(len(d['review']['supporting_evidence']) for d in drafts)==5;save(out/'draft-reviews.json',drafts);save(out/'source-paragraphs.json',sources);save(out/'COMPLETED.json',dict(status='verified-seven-SMR-and-five-HEIDI-primary-role-drafts-not-applied',primary_roles=12,supporting_pointers=5,current_reviews_preserved=len(prior['reviews']),source_pins={Path(__file__).resolve().relative_to(ROOT).as_posix():pin(Path(__file__))},drafts=pin(out/'draft-reviews.json'),paragraphs=pin(out/'source-paragraphs.json'),catalog_changed=False,implementation_credit=False,whole_goal_complete=False));print('Verified12 primary roles and5 supporting pointers; all932 current reviews unchanged')


if __name__=='__main__':
    if not __debug__:raise RuntimeError('Never disable primary source checks')
    main()
